# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never, under any circumstances, real client material.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# This block is first because it is the only one that matters. Everything else
# here is housekeeping; this is the rule the repository exists under. It is
# deliberately wider than it needs to be: the cost of ignoring a file you did
# want is one `git add -f`, and the cost of the other mistake is not
# recoverable once it is pushed.

transcripts/
transkripte/
sitzungen/
sessions/
*.real.*

# The formats a documentation assistant exports a session in. There is no
# reason for one of these to be in this repository, and every reason for a
# stray one not to be committed by accident.
*.docx
*.doc
*.pdf
*.vtt
*.srt
!samples/*.vtt
!samples/*.srt

# What this tool writes *about* transcripts. The export carries no names and no
# transcript lines (see `Korpus.export`), but it is still a year of one
# person's therapy in numbers, and it belongs on your machine and not here.
therapy-analysis-*.json
/report.json
/bericht.json
/befund.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyd
*.egg
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.python-version

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored Pyodide runtime — optional, large, fetched by the user.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# See "One foreign request" in the README. The tarball is ignored too: the
# README tells you to curl it into this directory, and 200 MB of runtime in a
# repository whose whole point is that it has no build step would be a joke.
vendor/
pyodide*.tar.bz2
pyodide*.tar.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors, tooling, operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.env
.env.*
